    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 all 30 tests pass with no failures or errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily create-limit rule for `POST /api/owners`: an owner is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners already have today's `registrationDate`.\n\nFollowing the existing city-capacity pattern (OfficeFloor function injection, not Spring MVC), I added:\n\n1. **`CheckDailyLimit.java`** (function) \u2014 counts persisted owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`; throws a checked `DailyLimitExceededException` at \u2265 100. Runs under `govern: [ transaction ]` so the count and insert share one consistent view, excluding the not-yet-saved owner.\n2. **`DailyLimitExceededException.java`** \u2014 checked exception carrying the count.\n3. **`DailyLimitExceededExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 global escalation handler responding 429 with a `ProblemDetail` body, matching the existing handlers.\n4. **`...DailyLimitExceededException.yml`** \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `checkDailyLimit` step between `checkCityCapacity` and `build`, inside the write transaction.\n\nThe new `Cp19Tests` (101st owner rejected) and pre-existing `Cp18Tests` (city capacity) both pass, and the full 30-test suite is green.",
